Ladybird’s UI process pushes the enabled extensions’ descriptors to
each WebContent process at launch and on every change, and a
process-wide ExtensionSet in WebContent keeps the latest set. WebKit
does the same through WebExtensionControllerProxy: the UI process’s
WebExtensionController sends each WebProcessProxy a
WebExtensionControllerParameters with every loaded context, and
WebExtensionContextProxy mirrors one context per process. Blink’s
ExtensionRegistry notifies every RenderProcessHost through
RendererStartupHelper::OnExtensionLoaded() and OnExtensionUnloaded(),
which send mojom::Renderer LoadExtensions and UnloadExtension, and
the renderer’s Dispatcher keeps the RendererExtensionRegistry. Gecko
registers a WebExtensionPolicy per extension in every process through
ExtensionPolicyService, with the parent’s ExtensionProcessScript
broadcasting the policies to content processes. The test-web flag
that loads fixture extensions for a run mirrors Chromium’s
--load-extension switch, which the extension browser tests use for
the same purpose.
